{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalIdeal","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RingConLiftAlgHom"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuot_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuot_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L120-L133","doc":"**The isomorphism is not between one-point algebras.**\n\n`AlgEquiv.ofBijective` would accept a bijection of trivial algebras just as happily, so this\nforecloses the vacuous reading structurally rather than by inspection: `wtrace 1 = 1 ≠ 0`,\nso `1` is not in the radical, so the class of `1` is not the class of `0`.  Its image\n`twoRowProduct 1 = 1` is therefore nonzero in `TwoRowBlocks n`, which also says the target\nis not the one-point ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuotEquiv_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuotEquiv_coe","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L113-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuotEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.traceQuotEquiv","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L97-L111","doc":"**`H_n(q) / rad(wtrace) ≅ ∏_{ℓ(λ) ≤ 2} M_{f^λ}(ℝ)`**, for every `n`, at convention D.\n\n`WtraceRadicalIdeal` supplied the two halves of the first isomorphism theorem; the missing\npiece was a lift out of a `RingCon` quotient.\n\n🛑 **Corrected:** an earlier version of this line credited `liftAlgHom` for supplying that\npiece.  It does not — `twoRowQuotHom`, which this is `AlgEquiv.ofBijective` of, is inlined\nagainst the corpus's algebra instances for the reason its own docstring gives, and\n`liftAlgHom` (now `QOU.MathlibExt.RingConLiftAlgHom.liftAlgHom`) is on no critical path\nhere.  The two statements contradicted each other fifty lines apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**Injective** by the ⊆ half of the kernel identity, **surjective** by\n`twoRowProduct_surjective`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom_coe","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L75-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.twoRowQuotHom","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L46-L73","doc":"The two-row projection, descended to the quotient.\n\n**Not** built from `RingConLiftAlgHom.liftAlgHom`, and the reason is a live instance collision rather\nthan a stylistic choice: there are **two** `Algebra ℝ` instances on this type — Mathlib's\n`RingCon.instAlgebraQuotient` and the corpus's own\n`QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.instAlgebraTraceQuot` — so `liftAlgHom`'s output (which picks\nMathlib's) and a signature written against `TraceQuot` (which picks the corpus's) are\ndifferent `AlgHom` types and do not unify.  Spelling the type as `.ringCon.Quotient` does\nnot help: `instAlgebraTraceQuot` matches whenever the ideal *is* a `traceRadicalIdeal`.\n`TwoRowBlocks` adds a second, smaller mismatch of the same kind (`Pi.semiring` against\n`Pi.ring.toSemiring`).  So this is inlined against the corpus's instances; `liftAlgHom`\nstays as the general-purpose piece in `QOU.MathlibExt.RingConLiftAlgHom`, which is\nwhat would go upstream.\n\nThat duplication is a defect in its own right and is **not fixed here** — changing which\ninstance the corpus uses is a behavioural change across every `quotMk` consumer, so it is\nrecorded rather than touched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.ringCon_iff_twoRowProduct_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.ringCon_iff_twoRowProduct_eq","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L35-L44","doc":"**Two elements are congruent mod the radical iff the two-row projection cannot tell them\napart.**  `traceRadicalIdeal_eq_ker` transported to the congruence; it is the hypothesis the\nlift needs, and in *both* directions at once, which is why it is stated as an iff. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.TwoRowBlocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalQuotient.TwoRowBlocks","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalQuotient.lean#L30-L33","doc":"The target of the two-row projection: one matrix block per at-most-two-row partition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}